# Raspberry Pi Pico
# Level 5 - Advanced
#
# One program idea, another board: a dimmer and a button on a Pico, using its GP pin names.
# You learn: that only the board line and the pin names change between boards - the rest is the same Mujard.
# You need: a Raspberry Pi Pico, a potentiometer on GP26 (ADC0), an LED + resistor on GP15 and a button from GP14 to GND.

board pico

onboard = pin LED as output
lamp    = pin GP15 as pwm
knob    = analog GP26
button  = pin GP14 as input pullup

var lamp_on = true

every 20 ms:
    if lamp_on:
        lamp.write(knob.percent)
    else:
        lamp.write(0 %)

on button.pressed:
    lamp_on = not lamp_on
    onboard.write(lamp_on)
    print "Lamp {lamp_on} on a {board.name} ({board.chip})"
